marchyo NEWS                                             -*- outline -*-

User-visible changes worth mentioning, newest first, after the GNU
Coding Standards (NEWS File).  marchyo has no versioned releases: each
release is named after its year and month (YYYY-MM), and changes are
grouped by that release.  CHANGELOG.md lists them in detail.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-11

  Hotkeys (breaking): the pre-4.5 marchyo layout is the only layout
  again, and marchyo.keyboard.legacyBinds is gone.  Super+L locks, apps
  sit on plain Super+letter, the panels on Super+Shift (V audio,
  N network, B power, M monitor, Q Control Center), the overview on
  Super+grave, the command menu on Super+Alt+Space and the emoji picker
  on Super+period.  Binds that only the 4.5 layout had moved to:

    Cycle workspace layout     Super+Ctrl+J (back: Super+Ctrl+Shift+J)
    Minimize to the drawer     Super+Alt+D
    Calculator (qalc)          Super+Alt+C
    Activity (btop)            Super+Alt+T
    Next background            Super+Ctrl+Space
    Toggle menu                Super+Ctrl+Shift+X
    Act on newest notification Super+Ctrl+Alt+comma

  Dictation toggles on Super+Ctrl+X and the compose key is the Menu key
  again (marchyo.keyboard.composeKey = "shift-caps" selects
  Shift+Caps Lock).  The default web apps keep their Super+Shift keys,
  GitHub on Super+Shift+G included.

  Options (breaking): options that only passed a value on to an
  upstream NixOS option are retired.  Renamed ones keep working with a
  warning (the marchyo. prefix is left out on the left):

    security.firewall.enable       -> networking.firewall.enable
    power.hibernation.resumeDevice -> boot.resumeDevice
    hardware.logitech.enable       -> programs.solaar.enable
    graphics.nvidia.open           -> hardware.nvidia.open
    graphics.nvidia.powerManagement
                         -> hardware.nvidia.powerManagement.enable
    graphics.nvidia.containerToolkit.enable
                         -> hardware.nvidia-container-toolkit.enable
    graphics.amd.overdrive.enable  -> hardware.amdgpu.overdrive.enable
    nix.router.{enable,port,netrcFile}
                         -> services.ncro.{enable,port,netrcFile}
    services.tailscale.enable      -> services.tailscale.enable
    services.localsend.{enable,openFirewall}
                         -> programs.localsend.{enable,openFirewall}

  Removed ones fail evaluation with a hint:
  marchyo.graphics.nvidia.package (set hardware.nvidia.package),
  marchyo.performance.kernel (boot.kernelPackages), marchyo.nix.caches
  (nix.settings.substituters), marchyo.nix.router.extraUpstreams and
  marchyo.users.<name>.uid and .name.

  Several GPUs (breaking for multi-GPU hosts): marchyo.graphics.primary
  names the GPU that drives the display.  Every listed vendor's drivers
  are installed, but only the primary sets the driver variables, and
  Hyprland renders on it first.  A host that lists more than one vendor
  must set it, unless it is a PRIME laptop with one integrated GPU,
  where it follows the PRIME mode.  An empty marchyo.graphics.vendors no
  longer assumes Intel.

  Home Manager (breaking): marchyo's Home Manager modules run only
  under the marchyo NixOS module, which sets them up for every
  marchyo.users entry.  There is no standalone Home Manager output any
  more (homeConfigurations, lib.mkHomeConfiguration).

  Installation: the flake exports the disko layouts
  (lib.diskoLayout, with nixosModules.disko) and the installer ISOs
  (packages.x86_64-linux.iso-minimal and iso-graphical, "just iso").

** New features

  Web app preset marchyo.webapps.presets.google adds the Google
  Workspace apps: Gmail, Calendar, Drive, Docs, Sheets, Slides, Meet,
  Chat, Keep, Forms, Sites, Contacts and Tasks.

  New panels: Bluetooth (Super+Ctrl+B), a speed test for network and
  disk (Super+Ctrl+Alt+P) and Dropbox (Super+Ctrl+Alt+D).  Breaking:
  Super+Ctrl+B used to start the bluetui manager; that is now
  Super+Ctrl+Shift+B while the shell is on.  Display tiles in the
  Display panel work from the keyboard.

  Bar: the middle of the bar has three sections, so widgets can sit
  beside the clock without moving it.  The recording, reminder,
  dictation, stay-awake and do-not-disturb indicators form one group,
  and tray icons can be pinned so the rest fold behind the "·" button.
  "marchyo bar put", "move", "remove" and "set" rearrange the bar
  without a rebuild, and "marchyo bar reset" undoes it.  Double-click
  empty bar space to change the bar background.

  Theme and wallpaper pickers: Super+Ctrl+T now opens a grid of theme
  previews instead of the launcher's theme mode, and Super+Ctrl+Shift+W
  opens the same grid for wallpapers.  Arrows move, Enter applies, Escape
  closes.  Marchyo draws four wallpaper patterns (grid, dots, bands,
  contour) per light and dark theme; "marchyo bg list" lists what you
  can choose, and a theme can list its own wallpapers.

  Fonts and appearance: "marchyo font set <family> --kind ui" changes
  the interface font of GTK and the shell as well as the terminal font.
  "marchyo theme gaps", "bar-position", "bar-background" and "icons"
  change window gaps, the bar placement, its background and the icon
  theme without a rebuild; the Control Center has an Appearance section
  for them.  Runtime theme, wallpaper, font and appearance changes now
  survive a rebuild until you revert them.

  More themed apps: btop, kitty, foot, alacritty, Helix, Neovim, Emacs,
  tmux and fcitx5 follow the theme.  marchyo.tmux.enable (on with
  marchyo.development.enable) gives a themed tmux.

  Command menu: Super+Alt+Space opens a searchable menu of everything
  marchyo can do (apps, capture, toggles, appearance, hardware, system,
  setup, share); Escape goes up a level.  Super+R opens the apps,
  Super+K the keybinding cheat sheet.  Add or hide entries with
  marchyo.menu.entries or ~/.config/marchyo/menu.local.json.

  Shell plugins: "marchyo plugin validate" checks a plugin checkout.

  Shell panels: panels opened with a key or "marchyo shell open" take
  keyboard focus.  Escape closes, Up, Down and Tab move between
  controls, Enter and Space activate.  The shell also has a native Ui
  kit and a dev gallery ("marchyo shell gallery") that shows it.

  Reduce motion at run time: "marchyo toggle reduce-motion on" makes
  every shell transition instant, and the shell follows Hyprland's
  animations setting.

  Notifications from scripts: "marchyo notify" takes the flags of
  omarchy-notification-send and can attach a click command and up to three
  buttons.  Toasts that were on screen come back after a shell restart,
  do-not-disturb is kept across restarts, and the notification centre
  works from the keyboard (Up, Down, Enter, Delete).  Only
  "marchyo notify" can attach a click command: each one carries a
  one-time token, and the shell checks it again when a notification is
  replaced.

  What changed and first-login setup: when Marchyo's NEWS changed, one
  notification opens a panel with the new entries and a summary of the
  last switch.  On the first login a welcome notification opens a setup
  checklist ("marchyo setup") for git, SSH, FIDO2, fingerprint, language,
  keyboard, theme and dictation.  Super+Ctrl+U and Super+Ctrl+H open the
  two panels.

  Notifications: toasts stack by sender into decks that expand on
  hover, show verification codes with a Copy button, and route clicks
  to the sender's window or link.  Do-not-disturb still lets through
  critical notifications, Marchyo's own and those carrying a code.

  Display panel: a shell panel (Super+Ctrl+D) for each display's
  brightness, scale, resolution, refresh rate and rotation, with a
  layout map to drag displays around and Extend or Mirror for the
  laptop panel.  Choices are kept per monitor in
  $XDG_STATE_HOME/marchyo/monitors/settings and survive rebuilds.
  "marchyo monitor reset" clears them, "marchyo monitor save --nix"
  prints the layout as marchyo.monitors, and
  marchyo.monitorPanel.persist = false ignores the file.

  Per-monitor workspaces: every monitor has its own workspaces 1-10,
  and Super+1..0 act on the focused monitor.  A monitor keeps its
  workspaces across unplugs, and the bar numbers each monitor's
  workspaces from 1.  Set marchyo.workspaces.perMonitor = false for
  one global set; "marchyo monitor workspaces reset" starts over.

  World clock and status indicators: the Elsewhen panel (Super+Ctrl+Alt+E)
  shows the time in your cities on a map.  Optional bar indicators show a
  pending update, a nearly full Nix store disk
  (marchyo.shell.diskWarnPercent) and failing "marchyo doctor" checks.
  The Power panel can roll back to the previous generation.

  Window appearance: marchyo.theme.appearance.transparency (opaque,
  transparent, glassy), corners (theme, sharp, rounded) and animations
  (auto, on, off) set how windows look.  "marchyo theme transparency",
  "marchyo theme corners" and "marchyo toggle animations" switch them
  live, and the Appearance menu groups them with theme, background and
  font.  "marchyo window pop" (Super+Alt+O) pops a tile out as a
  floating pinned window.

  Camera: WirePlumber now waits at login for camera access.

  Captive portals: NetworkManager now checks connectivity against
  nmcheck.gnome.org by default on desktops
  (marchyo.network.connectivityCheck; set enable = false to send no
  probes).  The shell marks restricted networks, and "marchyo network
  portal" or the Network panel opens the sign-in page.

  Power: marchyo.power.hibernation turns hibernation back on, with
  suspend-then-hibernate and a resume-device assertion.  marchyo.power.lid
  sets the lid-close action on battery, on AC and when docked.  Closing
  the lid with an external display connected turns the laptop panel off.

  Input methods: marchyo.keyboard.layouts accepts the ime values
  chewing (Zhuyin) and cangjie (Cangjie 5).  Input starts in Latin; a
  lone Shift toggles the engine and Super+I cycles layouts, then
  engines.  Noto CJK fonts follow the configured language.

  Keyboard: marchyo.keyboard.fnMode picks whether the top row sends
  media keys or F1-F12 by default, the keyboard backlight keys work
  through "marchyo brightness --keyboard", and composeKey can be
  "shift-caps" (Shift+Caps Lock composes, Caps Lock stays Caps Lock).

  GPU options: marchyo.graphics.nvidia.generation picks the default
  driver branch and open modules, and the NVIDIA Container Toolkit is
  on with development containers.  marchyo.graphics.amd adds ROCm and
  VA-API.  Hybrid laptops can add an "integrated-only" boot entry that
  turns the NVIDIA GPU off.

  Web app presets: marchyo.webapps.presets.m365 adds Outlook, Word,
  Excel, PowerPoint, Teams and OneDrive, and presets.notion adds Notion.

** Changes in behavior

  Defaults: the bar is a full-width strip
  (marchyo.theme.appearance.floatingBar = false), and input starts in
  Latin (marchyo.keyboard.autoActivateIME = false).

  The systemd-boot menu is hidden by default.  Hold Space at power-on to
  open it, or set boot.loader.timeout to show it.

  Faster menus and panels: the shell's keybinds reach it through
  Hyprland global shortcuts, so no process starts per keypress.

  Faster logout, reboot and shutdown: marchyo closes every window and
  waits at most two seconds for the apps before it ends the session.

  BBR congestion control with the fq qdisc is now the default on every
  host, not only with marchyo.performance.tuning.  Non-rotational disks
  use the kyber I/O scheduler; with tuning.nvme, NVMe disks keep
  mq-deadline.  marchyo.security.ssh adds a key-only SSH server that
  refuses to evaluate while a login user has no authorized key.

  The flake now has six inputs (nixpkgs, home-manager, treefmt-nix,
  ncro, tinted-schemes and disko), and the design system is part of
  marchyo instead of a separate input.

  OBS Studio and lazydocker are no longer installed.  The SUPER + ALT + D
  lazydocker bind is removed too.  Add the packages through
  environment.systemPackages if you want them.

** Removed features

  Breaking: this release removes the omarchy plugin layer (omarchy's
  first-party plugins, plugins that replace native panels, "marchyo
  plugin dev"), the AI tooling (marchyo.ai.*, "marchyo agent", the
  agents panel, the Quake console, "marchyo dev", local Ollama;
  marchyo.defaults.aiAgent still installs one agent CLI), unfree and
  unverified packages (Superwhisper, Hex, Amp, gliff and others), the
  speaker tuner, the Cam Link relay, Taildrop in "marchyo share", Slack
  theme injection, the VS Code, Obsidian, Slack and herdr theme
  surfaces, every shell and CLI language except English, nix-on-droid,
  the last nix-darwin pieces, sops-nix and the nixos-hardware re-export.
  Options that were removed fail evaluation with a pointer to what
  replaces them.  Dictation uses Voxtype only.

  The search demo page at marchyo.org/search was removed.

** Bug fixes

  Theme switching keeps btop and the desktop light/dark preference on
  the same saved selection after a rebuild.  A failed preference update
  reports an error and preserves the previous selection.  Chrome,
  Chromium and Brave now follow the light/dark switch too.

  The greeter follows every user's theme, not only the first one's,
  and "marchyo network portal" no longer closes unrelated windows
  when a portal redirects to a host name with pattern syntax in it.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-10

** New features

  Quickshell desktop shell: marchyo.shell provides a bar, launcher
  command palette, notification centre, Control Center, workspace
  overview, session lock and greeter in one themed shell.  It is
  enabled by default with marchyo.desktop.enable and replaces the
  separate bar, notification daemon, on-screen display and launcher.

  Runtime theming: themes switch live without a rebuild across the
  shell, Ghostty, Hyprland, GTK, Qt, bat, fzf, hyprlock and the console,
  and "marchyo theme generate" derives a palette from a wallpaper.

** Changes in behavior

  The design system moved to a Jost, Fira Sans and IBM Plex Mono look.

  The cache proxy listens on localhost only.

** Removed features

  Stylix, nix-darwin support, the Vicinae, noctalia, waybar, mako and
  SwayOSD modules were removed.  The gaming, kmscon, snapper and
  hibernation modules gave way to upstream NixOS options.

** Bug fixes

  Fixed Qt 6.12 turning shell colours black.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-09

** New features

  Typed options: marchyo.monitors declares the monitor layout, and
  marchyo.theme.appearance scales the shell's corners, animation speed
  and borders.

  Shell plugins: upstream omarchy Quickshell bar widgets run on the
  shell through a compatibility layer, managed with "marchyo plugin
  add", "list" and "remove".

** Changes in behavior

  Development tools default to rootless Podman.

** Removed features

  The marchyo.ai BYOK tooling was removed.

** Bug fixes

  Fixed Hyprland Lua-config breakage, shell and greeter crash loops,
  the black login screen and dconf conflicts on light-theme rebuilds.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-08

** New features

  Documentation: an end-user manual on the documentation site.

** Changes in behavior

  bash is the only login shell.

  Users no longer join the docker group by default.

** Removed features

  The self-tracking telemetry stack was removed.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-07

** New features

  marchyo CLI: a 1.0 command line with a frozen command surface for
  theme, toggle, capture, update, rollback, gc, diff, doctor, share,
  plugin and more, with shell completions and a man page.  Changes
  apply to the running desktop and are restored at startup.

  Omarchy-style desktop: central and power menus, dictation with
  Whisper, web apps with launch keys, screensaver, do-not-disturb,
  caffeine, and fingerprint and FIDO2 login.

  Documentation: a Starlight site with option and package reference.

  marchyo.theme.fontScale scales every text surface.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-05

** Changes in behavior

  The default keyboard layout is us(altgr-intl) with Compose on the
  Menu key.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-04

** Changes in behavior

  Ghostty is the default terminal.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-03

** New features

  marchyo.defaults picks the browser, editors, players, file manager
  and email client.

** Changes in behavior

  Security defaults tightened: CPU mitigations stay on unless
  marchyo.performance.disableMitigations is set, and
  accept-flake-config is no longer enabled.

* Noteworthy changes in 2026-01

** New features

  GPU vendor options for Intel, AMD and NVIDIA, with NVIDIA PRIME
  offload, sync and reverse-sync modes.

* Noteworthy changes in 2025-11

** New features

  fcitx5 input methods with Chinese, Japanese and Korean support under
  marchyo.keyboard.layouts.

* Noteworthy changes in 2025-10

** New features

  Installation tooling: installer ISOs, disko layouts, workstation and
  minimal flake templates, and marchyo.lib.mkNixosSystem.

  Theming through nix-colors Base16 schemes with the Modus schemes.

  Optional Prometheus and Grafana monitoring, system hardening and
  BTRFS root rollback.

** Changes in behavior

  The legacy base, desktop and developer profiles were removed;
  desktop and development settings now follow their enable options.

* Noteworthy changes in 2025-09

** New features

  First version of the NixOS and Home Manager module set for a
  Hyprland desktop, with marchyo.* options for users and desktop,
  development, media and office feature flags.
